ose  performances draw you into the comic and  tragic sides of Finley's drama it all  lends an exacting edge to the film's  final moments which may leave you  giggling while also fighting a nasty  chill in your spine core leaf RJ's debut  feature set in the sweltering Moroccan  desert is proof that revenge is not  always a dish best served  old port survival story and part tale of  righteous vengeance revenge unfolds in a  blood-soaked narrative that uses the  desert setting to serve up a steamy  helping a primal payback it begins when  pampered American party girl Jen's get  away with Richard is interrupted after  his pals show up early for a hunting  trip the weekend pivots dramatically  after a deplorable act that leads  Richard to leave Jen for dead in the  unforgiving desert she awakes to find  herself in the midst of a deadly cat and  mouse chase transformed from object to  Avenger leading to one of the best  hunters become the hunted narratives in  recent memory it's brutal bloody and  inventive in ways we can't go into  without spoiling the fun just know that  the almost dialogue free action is  guided to a final showdown that will  leave you absolutely shaken to the core  every so often we get a scary movie that  transcends its genre roots this year  that movie is unquestionably re Astor's  utterly terrifying family drama  hereditary the less you know going in  the better but we can't say that this  film begins dark and aster spends the  next hour tightening the screws to an  unbearable sense of atmospheric dread  before hitting you with one of the most  shocking moments and horror movie  history you'll never see it coming it'll  shock you in ways you've probably never  experienced in a movie and as impossible  as it may seem when it happens  hereditary then sets about getting a  whole lot darker if you're tough enough  to stick with it you'll be able to brag  to friends that you made it through one  of the best most disturbing horror films  not just the 2018 but likely of all time  unfolding and a beautifully realised  alternate version of present-day  Oakland sorry to bother you follows the  story of a young black telemarketer who  experiences a meteoric rise to success  after uncovering his inner white voice  as always we'll be getting that out to  you right away what follows is a  hilarious often horrifying madcap farce  that plays like a mash-up of Being John  Malkovich and get out  only angrier and more perceptive sorry  to bother you maybe chocked full of  comically inspired moments but it's  absolutely venomous in its presentation  of gender and race relations and  economic structures and it never misses  a beat as it pivots effortlessly from  one shocking moment to the next director  boots Riley's cast doesn't  Abid either and they keep Riley's  politically charged sci-fi Fantasia  grounded in particularly hard-hitting  ways though it may leave you wincing the  next time you see a horse man Luca  Guadagnino Suspiria is a fresh ferocious  and surprisingly political take on Dario  Argento's bloody brooding 1977 horror  classic the newest version of the  twisted tale about an enigmatic dancer  being tormented by Dark Horse's  actually best the film that inspired it  in both scope and scares Suspiria s--  2018 version also dances past Argento's  original and runtime clocking in at a  hefty 152 minutes and is filled with  welcome narrative additions like  character development and actual dancing  it also tends to avoid blind bloodlust  in favor of mood and Menace as well  ratcheting up the tension with fiery  flourishes of nightmarish imagery that  punctuate the gruesome acts of violence  throughout even if you've seen Argento  Suspiria you won't be prepared for the  gritty grisly carnage Guadagnino brings  to the table making his take not just  one of the most ambitious ly unsettling  remakes ever produced but also one of  the best Mandy is a film whose atypical  revenge narrative certainly fits the  b-movie mold even as it mercilessly  transcends expectations made even better  by the fact that Nicolas Cage plays a  man hell-bent on avenging the murder of  his lover somehow Mandy ended up being  one of the most memorable films and  cages filmography  it's crazy evil is what director Panos  cosmatos does with this construct that  makes the film so uniquely disquieting  peppering the action with a murderous  cult of hippies led by a folk singing  wannabe demigod throw in a demonic biker  gang hallucinatory narcotics  surrealistic imagery and enough fake  blood to float an ark and you've earned  a spot in the vaunted cult classic canon  yes Mandy is every bit the b-movie it  seems but it's also one of the most  visually striking vividly realized and  wholly original films of the year and  it's unbridled insanity simply must be  seen to be believed  caged crazier than usual crazier than  this  [Music]  [Applause]  now that st. something.when author Jeff  Vandermeer published anihilation it  became an instant classic of modern  science fiction literature and an easy  target for a big screen adaptation fans  of the book were even more excited when  hearing that Alex Garland was handling  that adaptation after months of delays  and behind-the-scenes troubles  annihilation finally arrived in theaters  except it didn't exactly stick to the  source material garland took some  serious liberties with the story to  cramp the narrative all his own but his  annihilation works as both a direct  adaptation and a wholly original story  that's every bit as effective horrifying  and emotionally charged as the book  garland even best Van der Meers source  material when it comes to scares with a  blood-curdling bear woman beast that  serves as one of the most unsettling  creature creations of this or any year  if only garland had left the door open  for a sequel we might have gotten to see  even more his haunting unearthly  delights with no fewer than a couple  dozen or so films utilizing social  medias like share obsession as a plot  device  Robert McClure sobering drama like me is  nothing like the rest  in fact this incisive feature debut is  not like any film you've ever seen  before from its jarring opening moments  mock lers film is clearly out to shock  his tragic tale of a young woman  broadcasting her crime spree across  social media is part road movie part  hallucinatory crime thriller opening  with an attention-grabbing heist and  ending with brutal violence the moments  in between find a hushed and harried  character study vivid photography and  kaleidoscopic editing ensure that even  the film's muted moments come and go  with galvanizing energy that manic mix  of styles makes like me the sort of  soul-crushing spirited film you simply  cannot unsee so make sure that you do  after unleashing his sweaty palm action  epic the raid in 2011 and following it  up with the equally bonkers the raid -  Gareth Evans proved himself to be a  master of both staging and human drama  so there was good reason to be excited  when Netflix announced they'd be  producing Evans's new film apostle which  saw the director tackling the horror  genre the result was a  riah thriller about a troubled man  tasked with retrieving his sister from a  creepy island dwelling religious cult  who worship a bloodthirsty deity for the  first hour the movie swings a  hypnotically unholy pendulum before  viewers eyes giving apostle linear  suffocating gothic energy and then evan  spends the next hour smashing that  pendulum into bloody bits making you  long for time when a bloodthirsty deity  was all you had to fear expect dastardly  deeds unspeakably gruesome acts  fantastically grotesque imagery and a  soul choking sense of dread  you'll be glued to the screen for every  nightmarish moment we're in a virtual  Golden Age of genre mashups and one  amazing example of this is that  gloriously unhinged World War 2 horror  thriller Overlord few other 2018 films  arrive as well-equipped 